                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/255: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva (Gilbert) to the Acting Secretary
                            of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-05-14T18:00:00+01:00">May 14, 1932—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 14—5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>190. From Reber. My telegram 189, May 14,
                    5 p.m.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d528-f1"/> The statement I made in the Committee
                    this morning was along the following lines:</p>
                <p>[Here follows the substance of the first two paragraphs of Department’s telegram
                    No. 77, May 8, 1 p.m., printed on <ref target="#pg723">page 723</ref>.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
